WEBVTT

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:12.940
Okay, attention please?

00:00:12.940 --> 00:00:15.130
Some of you may have already noticed,

00:00:15.130 --> 00:00:18.320
but there's this little dot here.

00:00:18.320 --> 00:00:20.830
Kind of like a secondary 
sex characteristic.

00:00:20.830 --> 00:00:24.550
But it's not pronounced 
Gintama Dash or Dot.

00:00:24.550 --> 00:00:26.660
Due to grown-up circumstances,

00:00:26.660 --> 00:00:28.340
there has to be something here.

00:00:28.340 --> 00:00:30.030
Because grown-ups grow hair down there.

00:00:30.030 --> 00:00:32.480
But it's still pronounced Gintama.

00:00:32.980 --> 00:00:35.450
Grown-ups keep their mouths shut

00:00:35.450 --> 00:00:37.080
when someone's unshaven.

00:00:37.520 --> 00:00:41.660
So with that lesson learned, 
let's try this again.

00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:26.400
<b>Snack Otose</b>

00:02:24.370 --> 00:02:26.390
Apparently, she's got herself...

00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:30.200
...a man.

00:02:32.390 --> 00:02:34.450
<b>I noticed that Catherine was behaving</b>

00:02:34.450 --> 00:02:35.990
<b>rather oddly lately.</b>

00:02:35.990 --> 00:02:37.410
<b>That explains why.</b>

00:02:37.850 --> 00:02:40.440
So, did someone lose a bet or something?

00:02:40.440 --> 00:02:42.360
He's a regular here.

00:02:42.360 --> 00:02:44.920
They've been on friendly 
terms for a while.

00:02:44.920 --> 00:02:47.350
No, seriously. This guy must have lost

00:02:47.350 --> 00:02:48.430
This defies logic.

00:02:48.430 --> 00:02:50.590
No man would ever be interested 
in that nasty woman.

00:02:50.910 --> 00:02:54.840
Clearly, she was the result 
of a bad joke by God.

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:57.270
If he threw together some 
leftover cat and housewife parts

00:02:57.270 --> 00:02:59.310
to make a present for his grandchild,

00:02:59.750 --> 00:03:01.620
which was then relegated

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:04.920
to chew toy duty, that would be her.

00:03:05.610 --> 00:03:07.330
But don't you think that

00:03:07.330 --> 00:03:09.270
Catherine-san looks prettier these days?

00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:10.290
How?

00:03:10.310 --> 00:03:12.430
You mean how the cat and 
housewife parts fit together?

00:03:12.430 --> 00:03:14.180
That's because God files 
the edges and gives the

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.280
putty plenty of time to dry.

00:03:15.930 --> 00:03:17.110
According to my data,

00:03:17.110 --> 00:03:18.130
women become more beautiful

00:03:18.130 --> 00:03:19.660
when they fall in love.

00:03:19.650 --> 00:03:20.580
What?

00:03:20.580 --> 00:03:22.830
That's just lip service.

00:03:23.120 --> 00:03:24.530
Don't they tend to place their

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:26.610
hand on their cheek and sigh?

00:03:26.610 --> 00:03:28.440
Just stop already.

00:03:28.440 --> 00:03:32.230
Women, old and robot, 
always love this topic.

00:03:32.230 --> 00:03:35.130
My folder of love stories 
is ten yottabytes.

00:03:35.130 --> 00:03:36.410
That's ridiculously huge!

00:03:36.850 --> 00:03:38.040
Listen to me.

00:03:38.040 --> 00:03:39.960
You can putty up a Zaku 
as much as you want.

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:41.820
It's never going to become a Gundam.

00:03:41.820 --> 00:03:43.160
Fix your data.

00:03:43.160 --> 00:03:44.190
Understood.

00:03:44.190 --> 00:03:47.860
Master Gintoki can never 
be like Hiro Mizushima.

00:03:47.860 --> 00:03:49.440
Gajiro Sato is the best he can manage.

00:03:49.440 --> 00:03:52.200
What's with the cruel gap 
in wavy hair characters?

00:03:52.460 --> 00:03:54.200
I'm back.

00:03:54.500 --> 00:03:56.480
Look, the Zaku's back.

00:03:56.480 --> 00:03:58.720
Tune her up, mechanic.

00:03:58.720 --> 00:04:01.060
Sorry I took so long.

00:04:01.060 --> 00:04:02.450
There was an elderly person

00:04:02.450 --> 00:04:04.530
who needed help carrying something.

00:04:05.160 --> 00:04:07.750
Please deduct it from my wages.

00:04:10.590 --> 00:04:13.450
Z-ZZZ Gundam has returned!

00:04:13.450 --> 00:04:14.880
Didn't I explain this to you?

00:04:14.880 --> 00:04:17.020
Explain what?!

00:04:17.020 --> 00:04:19.690
Her physique is completely different!

00:04:19.690 --> 00:04:22.970
You can't pin this on an 
idiosyncratic animator!

00:04:22.970 --> 00:04:23.810
Oh, Gintoki-san.

00:04:23.810 --> 00:04:25.100
Welcome.

00:04:25.330 --> 00:04:26.880
Enjoy yourself.

00:04:26.880 --> 00:04:29.070
Even her personality has been Newtype'd!

00:04:29.560 --> 00:04:31.810
Why is she so polite now?!

00:04:31.810 --> 00:04:34.360
Love can't change a girl this much!

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:36.150
Wait, love...?

00:04:36.150 --> 00:04:38.370
You all know?

00:04:38.730 --> 00:04:40.450
Oh, I'm so embarrassed!

00:04:40.450 --> 00:04:41.440
I'm sorry.

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.090
I planned to tell you

00:04:43.090 --> 00:04:45.340
once everything was settled...

00:04:45.770 --> 00:04:47.410
Everything was settled?

00:04:47.650 --> 00:04:49.380
Catherine, are you...

00:04:50.230 --> 00:04:52.630
Otose-san, I'm...

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:58.890
<b>Snack Otose</b>

00:04:54.120 --> 00:04:55.680
...in a relationship with

00:04:55.680 --> 00:04:57.740
someone who wants to marry me.

00:04:58.890 --> 00:05:04.850
<b>It's Too Confusing When Talking About the Poster Girl for a Poster Store, So Call Her a Sandwich Board</b>

00:05:06.140 --> 00:05:08.070
Suejiro Suemoto-san.

00:05:08.070 --> 00:05:10.080
A regular at Otose-san's place.

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.430
That's how he got to know Catherine-san.

00:05:12.900 --> 00:05:14.660
He's an up-and-coming entrepreneur

00:05:14.660 --> 00:05:16.910
with considerable influence.

00:05:16.910 --> 00:05:18.480
Hmm...

00:05:18.480 --> 00:05:21.050
There are some real weirdos out there.

00:05:18.910 --> 00:05:27.420
<b>Sugar Content</b>

00:05:21.470 --> 00:05:23.360
People have always sucked up

00:05:23.360 --> 00:05:25.470
to him because of his money,

00:05:25.470 --> 00:05:27.420
so Catherine-san was like 
a breath of fresh air.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:33.670
Catherine-san!

00:05:35.170 --> 00:05:36.680
Sorry about being late.

00:05:37.180 --> 00:05:38.800
Please don't worry about it.

00:05:38.800 --> 00:05:40.930
You should wipe off your sweat first.

00:05:41.180 --> 00:05:44.180
Oh, thank you. I appreciate it.

00:05:47.230 --> 00:05:47.940
Ah!

00:05:50.440 --> 00:05:54.440
(My, Suejiro-san is so bold.)

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:58.450
<b>Flower House</b>

00:05:58.450 --> 00:06:00.450
Oh, dear. My head is spinning.

00:06:00.450 --> 00:06:01.450
This is so much fun.

00:06:03.580 --> 00:06:04.080
Ah!

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:04.700
Whoa...!

00:06:05.950 --> 00:06:06.830
Catherine-san...

00:06:06.960 --> 00:06:07.960
Suejiro-san...

00:06:10.890 --> 00:06:11.710
Wait a second.

00:06:12.500 --> 00:06:14.710
Is this the right show?

00:06:15.060 --> 00:06:18.720
Who wants to see them 
fawn over each other?

00:06:18.930 --> 00:06:21.770
Gin-san, we should be happy for them.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:22.890
That would be the grown-up response.

00:06:22.890 --> 00:06:23.430
Hah!

00:06:23.430 --> 00:06:24.290
Grown-up!

00:06:24.290 --> 00:06:24.880
Yeah, yeah.

00:06:24.880 --> 00:06:25.980
So sorry!

00:06:26.540 --> 00:06:29.510
In any case, business is 
booming at Snack Otose.

00:06:29.840 --> 00:06:32.460
It must be the charm of 
a new wife or something,

00:06:32.460 --> 00:06:34.730
since Catherine-san has 
doubled her clientele.

00:06:35.230 --> 00:06:37.180
And Suejiro-san seems 
like a nice person.

00:06:37.180 --> 00:06:39.240
He was a regular customer,

00:06:39.630 --> 00:06:42.130
so he isn't going to tell 
her to stop working.

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:43.240
Hmph!

00:06:43.510 --> 00:06:45.020
Make sure you don't fall

00:06:45.020 --> 00:06:46.400
for a woman like her, Sadaharu!

00:06:46.400 --> 00:06:48.490
You never know when she's gonna

00:06:48.490 --> 00:06:50.000
turn back into a chew toy.

00:07:40.380 --> 00:07:43.390
<b>Sugar Content</b>

00:07:41.190 --> 00:07:42.870
He lost all of his assets

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:45.010
when Lehman Brothers went bankrupt.

00:07:45.460 --> 00:07:47.060
So he was saying that he can

00:07:47.060 --> 00:07:48.640
no longer make Catherine-san happy...

00:07:48.800 --> 00:07:50.680
So he wants to call it off?

00:07:50.680 --> 00:07:52.970
Just goes to show that he's a man with

00:07:52.970 --> 00:07:54.060
no money and no balls.

00:07:54.060 --> 00:07:56.650
But Catherine-san refused.

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:59.820
She said that she would support him.

00:07:59.820 --> 00:08:00.570
Huh?

00:08:01.370 --> 00:08:04.470
Suejiro-san has a piece 
of property left that

00:08:04.470 --> 00:08:05.600
isn't in the Kabuki district.

00:08:05.600 --> 00:08:07.310
He's going to open a new business there.

00:08:08.060 --> 00:08:09.660
With Catherine-san.

00:08:09.930 --> 00:08:11.390
So what?

00:08:11.390 --> 00:08:12.790
That thief who showed up in

00:08:12.790 --> 00:08:14.220
episode 12 of this anime,

00:08:14.220 --> 00:08:17.640
is finally leaving in episode 206?

00:08:17.640 --> 00:08:19.420
Well, it's like she's graduating,

00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:21.460
becoming independent.

00:08:23.000 --> 00:08:25.260
Otose-san will be a little lonely,

00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:27.030
but I'm sure that she'll be the first

00:08:27.030 --> 00:08:28.500
one to congratulate them.

00:08:30.490 --> 00:08:31.500
Master Gintoki.

00:08:31.500 --> 00:08:33.600
There is an emergency.

00:08:33.600 --> 00:08:36.190
Could you come see Ms. 
Otose immediately?

00:08:38.680 --> 00:08:41.720
Uh, I have a little 
emergency of my own here.

00:08:41.720 --> 00:08:43.570
Could you leave immediately?

00:08:43.570 --> 00:08:45.090
I will take over here.

00:08:45.090 --> 00:08:46.200
Take over what?

00:08:46.200 --> 00:09:02.210
<b>Keep the bathroom clean!</b>

00:08:46.840 --> 00:08:49.210
Go see Ms. Otose now.

00:08:49.210 --> 00:08:51.080
After walking through the cold,

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:54.130
I'm at terminal velocity, 
or diarrhea city.

00:08:54.130 --> 00:08:55.390
I have retrieved the appropriate data.

00:08:55.390 --> 00:08:58.610
I simply need to continue 
making ice cream, correct?

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:00.020
Chocolate.

00:09:00.020 --> 00:09:02.210
And make sure it doesn't 
fall off the cone.

00:09:03.010 --> 00:09:04.010
Man...

00:09:04.010 --> 00:09:05.970
What's going on?

00:09:06.220 --> 00:09:07.710
She probably wants to talk about

00:09:07.710 --> 00:09:09.470
Catherine-san and Suejiro-san's future?

00:09:12.280 --> 00:09:13.310
-Gin-chan!
-Gin-San!

00:09:13.310 --> 00:09:14.140
Catherine!

00:09:14.140 --> 00:09:15.270
Are you okay?!

00:09:16.560 --> 00:09:17.860
What was that for?!

00:09:18.300 --> 00:09:19.740
Otose-san!

00:09:20.800 --> 00:09:23.150
If you want to leave, scram.

00:09:23.570 --> 00:09:26.660
I won't object or try to stop you.

00:09:27.820 --> 00:09:29.600
But I can't stand

00:09:29.600 --> 00:09:32.570
to watch people like you who dream

00:09:32.570 --> 00:09:36.330
and can't keep their feet on the ground.

00:09:36.800 --> 00:09:39.110
You can call me whatever you want!

00:09:39.110 --> 00:09:40.790
But are you really saying that

00:09:40.790 --> 00:09:42.360
Catherine's hopes are 
just a pipe dream?!

00:09:42.360 --> 00:09:43.610
Otose-san...

00:09:43.610 --> 00:09:44.420
Catherine!

00:09:44.890 --> 00:09:48.370
I've been saving up money

00:09:49.050 --> 00:09:52.430
so I might open my own bar one day...

00:09:52.430 --> 00:09:54.930
<b>Snack Otose</b>

00:09:53.680 --> 00:09:55.100
I wanted to create a place

00:09:55.460 --> 00:09:58.400
like this one, where 
everyone was all smiles.

00:10:00.090 --> 00:10:05.440
I wanted to become a 
selfless person like you...

00:10:08.750 --> 00:10:10.400
I see how it is, Suejiro-san.

00:10:10.750 --> 00:10:12.440
I was wondering how you could

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:13.720
afford to open a new business.

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:15.370
That explains it.

00:10:15.700 --> 00:10:18.030
Don't say that!

00:10:18.350 --> 00:10:21.300
I just want to work together 
for our future...!

00:10:21.700 --> 00:10:24.540
Go ahead and get married, 
be independent.

00:10:25.030 --> 00:10:27.610
You don't need permission from me.

00:10:28.030 --> 00:10:31.430
We're total strangers, after all.

00:10:33.200 --> 00:10:34.520
Or is there more?

00:10:34.860 --> 00:10:38.360
You came here because you wanted to

00:10:38.910 --> 00:10:41.980
weasel money out of me and Catherine?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:43.230
Otose-san!

00:10:43.230 --> 00:10:44.340
That's crossing the line...

00:10:44.720 --> 00:10:45.990
Always...

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:50.410
I always thought of you as my mother...

00:10:52.430 --> 00:10:54.760
Fine, you old hag!

00:10:54.760 --> 00:10:56.780
I don't need your permission!

00:10:56.780 --> 00:11:00.290
And I'm never coming back to see you!

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.800
Roll over and die!

00:11:02.800 --> 00:11:04.090
That's nice.

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:05.740
I feel a lot better knowing that I won't

00:11:05.740 --> 00:11:07.010
have to see your face again!

00:11:07.370 --> 00:11:08.590
Wait up, hag!

00:11:08.590 --> 00:11:09.470
I'm not finished with you...

00:11:10.390 --> 00:11:12.380
I'll give you that instead of money.

00:11:12.380 --> 00:11:14.010
You can display it in your bar.

00:11:14.330 --> 00:11:15.730
It'll be the perfect place to display

00:11:15.730 --> 00:11:16.820
a cheap bottle of alcohol.

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:17.750
You old hag!

00:11:17.750 --> 00:11:19.090
I'll make you eat your words!

00:11:19.090 --> 00:11:20.980
I'll start up a bar that beats

00:11:20.980 --> 00:11:22.880
the crap out of this run-down place!

00:11:22.880 --> 00:11:26.450
I'll become bigger than you ever will!

00:11:26.450 --> 00:11:28.200
Goddamn!

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:28.200
Catherine!

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:28.890
Catherine!

00:11:28.890 --> 00:11:29.940
Catherine-san!

00:11:29.940 --> 00:11:31.670
Hey, you thief!

00:11:31.670 --> 00:11:33.690
Catherine!

00:11:47.000 --> 00:11:50.510
<b>Kabuki District Station</b>

00:11:48.360 --> 00:11:50.510
Write us a letter once 
you're settled down.

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:54.350
And invite us over 
once your bar is open.

00:11:54.350 --> 00:11:56.010
We'll all come to visit.

00:11:56.260 --> 00:11:59.240
Let me know if anything comes up.

00:11:59.240 --> 00:12:01.110
I will be right there.

00:12:01.110 --> 00:12:02.520
Thank you very much.

00:12:02.720 --> 00:12:05.300
Sorry that this isn't 
much of a send-off...

00:12:05.300 --> 00:12:07.810
Where did Gin-san run off to this time?

00:12:08.080 --> 00:12:09.280
Hey, Kagura-chan!

00:12:09.760 --> 00:12:12.070
You should say goodbye.

00:12:12.070 --> 00:12:14.280
Don't come back!

00:12:14.280 --> 00:12:15.780
Come on, Kagura-chan!

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.290
But if it's too much to take...

00:12:19.160 --> 00:12:22.300
If you can't put up with the in-laws,

00:12:22.300 --> 00:12:25.040
you can come back after 
raking him for alimony.

00:12:25.310 --> 00:12:27.170
You'll be more than welcome then.

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:36.300
Really, thank you for everything.

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.860
Please take care...

00:12:40.510 --> 00:12:42.530
Catherine-san, uh...
About Otose-san...

00:12:42.530 --> 00:12:45.190
The train on Platform 2
will be departing momentarily.

00:12:45.590 --> 00:12:47.210
I'll be going then.

00:12:47.720 --> 00:12:50.280
Suejiro-san is waiting for me.

00:12:50.540 --> 00:12:52.810
Please wait, Catherine-san!

00:12:53.950 --> 00:12:55.820
Please take care of...

00:12:57.210 --> 00:12:58.390
...Otose-san for me.

00:13:01.330 --> 00:13:03.830
<b>Snack Otose</b>

00:13:05.750 --> 00:13:07.970
Didn't you read the sign?

00:13:07.970 --> 00:13:09.570
We're closed today.

00:13:09.570 --> 00:13:10.600
Really?

00:13:10.600 --> 00:13:12.180
Guess you don't have a choice

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:13.800
without your poster girl around.

00:13:14.510 --> 00:13:16.190
Don't worry.

00:13:16.190 --> 00:13:18.160
I'm not here for a drink.

00:13:18.160 --> 00:13:19.350
I'm here to do the pouring.

00:13:30.960 --> 00:13:32.560
I never knew.

00:13:34.400 --> 00:13:36.260
When I first met her,

00:13:36.260 --> 00:13:38.370
she was just a dirty thief.

00:13:38.660 --> 00:13:41.290
I felt so bad for her

00:13:41.590 --> 00:13:43.970
that I let her stay at my bar.

00:13:43.970 --> 00:13:47.960
But she kept wandering off.

00:13:48.770 --> 00:13:50.070
Couldn't really blame her

00:13:50.070 --> 00:13:52.380
since she was a stray at heart,

00:13:53.430 --> 00:13:56.480
but lately, she's settled down

00:13:56.480 --> 00:13:59.350
and been working hard.

00:14:00.320 --> 00:14:03.660
I never knew she actually 
had a plan for her future...

00:14:04.180 --> 00:14:06.400
You didn't like the guy?

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.910
I should be grateful

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.480
that anyone was willing to take her.

00:14:11.880 --> 00:14:14.450
I understand that she 
can't exactly be choosy.

00:14:14.680 --> 00:14:16.990
Still, as a parent...

00:14:17.840 --> 00:14:20.700
Your daughter can bring 
home the perfect man

00:14:20.700 --> 00:14:22.990
and you'll still be able 
to find something wrong.

00:14:23.690 --> 00:14:25.670
I can't just smile and send her off,

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:28.660
when I know she's going to suffer.

00:14:29.430 --> 00:14:33.500
That was the best I could manage.

00:14:34.430 --> 00:14:35.950
I feel bad.

00:14:36.320 --> 00:14:38.750
So this is how it ends.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:45.100
If you feel bad, don't 
talk like it's over.

00:14:46.390 --> 00:14:50.080
Once she's opened a bar 
that's as good as this one,

00:14:50.080 --> 00:14:51.090
you should go have a drink.

00:14:59.240 --> 00:15:02.260
Catherine, find your happiness.

00:15:08.120 --> 00:15:10.920
The last train is departing.

00:15:14.420 --> 00:15:17.880
Today's service has concluded.

00:15:18.380 --> 00:15:24.390
Please exit the station 
in a swift manner.

00:15:44.150 --> 00:15:45.560
Suemoto?

00:15:45.800 --> 00:15:47.130
Nope, never heard of him.

00:15:47.640 --> 00:15:49.960
I don't think there's anybody 
by that name in this area.

00:15:50.400 --> 00:15:51.460
A bar?

00:15:51.710 --> 00:15:53.010
No, no.

00:15:53.010 --> 00:15:56.470
They're going to open a drugstore here.

00:15:57.960 --> 00:16:00.420
<b>Greater Edo Bank</b>

00:16:00.420 --> 00:16:02.180
<b>Please wait.</b>

00:16:02.180 --> 00:16:03.430
<b>Your balance is 0 yen.
Would you like a receipt?</b>

00:16:16.490 --> 00:16:18.540
Please remove your card.

00:16:32.330 --> 00:16:34.000
Are you new here?

00:16:34.440 --> 00:16:36.110
I don't know what you've been through,

00:16:36.110 --> 00:16:38.330
but it's a harsh world out there.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:42.750
If you need anything, let me know.

00:16:42.750 --> 00:16:45.380
They call me the lord of this park.

00:16:45.950 --> 00:16:48.720
I'll do anything for a little alcohol...

00:16:49.770 --> 00:16:51.270
<b>Bacchus</b>

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:51.270
W-Wait!

00:16:51.270 --> 00:16:54.810
Wh-Where did you get this stuff?!

00:16:54.810 --> 00:16:56.060
Don't touch that!

00:16:56.060 --> 00:16:58.770
L-Lady, that's incredible stuff!

00:16:58.990 --> 00:17:01.170
Bacchus wine from Planet Bacchus,

00:17:01.170 --> 00:17:04.280
only made once every hundred years!

00:17:07.280 --> 00:17:08.650
Legendary stuff that

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:10.720
will net hundreds from any collector!

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:14.780
H-How did you get your hands on this?!

00:17:16.080 --> 00:17:17.910
You can display it in your bar.

00:17:18.180 --> 00:17:20.760
The perfect place to display 
a cheap bottle of alcohol.

00:17:23.060 --> 00:17:26.260
Otose-san...

00:17:26.610 --> 00:17:29.690
You were giving me a push in the back...

00:17:30.750 --> 00:17:33.580
I'm so sorry, Otose-san...

00:17:35.290 --> 00:17:40.260
I have no place to display 
this wonderful bottle...

00:17:40.260 --> 00:17:41.950
Wait, I didn't drink any!

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.200
I didn't even take a sip!

00:17:43.200 --> 00:17:44.700
I just touched the bottle!

00:17:44.990 --> 00:17:46.960
I'm sorry! Really sorry!

00:17:47.200 --> 00:17:49.270
Sorry! I'm sorry!

00:17:49.270 --> 00:17:49.780
Okay?

00:17:54.920 --> 00:17:56.330
So yeah.

00:17:57.160 --> 00:17:58.760
She wouldn't tell me

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.350
what happened when I asked.

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.810
She kept saying that she

00:18:02.810 --> 00:18:05.290
couldn't go back because she promised.

00:18:05.760 --> 00:18:08.090
I guess she got sick 
of me asking questions,

00:18:08.090 --> 00:18:09.990
since she just ran off.

00:18:11.570 --> 00:18:13.600
Do you know anything, Gin-san?

00:18:14.890 --> 00:18:16.340
Hasegawa-san...

00:18:16.850 --> 00:18:20.360
Were your parents happy 
when you got married?

00:18:20.810 --> 00:18:22.920
Where did that come from?

00:18:23.380 --> 00:18:25.480
I married into money.

00:18:25.480 --> 00:18:28.170
So my whole family was thrilled.

00:18:28.550 --> 00:18:29.870
I see...

00:18:31.070 --> 00:18:33.370
That's what matters in the end.

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:38.220
Hey, it's starting, Gin-san!

00:18:38.220 --> 00:18:39.460
Whoa, wait!

00:18:39.460 --> 00:18:40.730
Wh-What?!

00:18:40.730 --> 00:18:42.440
Man, that's nasty!

00:18:42.950 --> 00:18:44.020
Gin-san!

00:18:44.020 --> 00:18:45.300
Look at that!

00:18:45.300 --> 00:18:46.380
What?

00:18:48.120 --> 00:18:49.010
Huh?

00:18:49.890 --> 00:18:52.890
<b>Easy Financing
Evil Loans</b>

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.890
You actually got the money.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.400
I knew you could do it.

00:18:55.400 --> 00:18:57.170
You just have to trick a few women

00:18:57.170 --> 00:18:58.850
and you can pay back 
your loan in no time.

00:18:58.850 --> 00:19:13.120
<b>Evil 4 Lyfe</b>

00:18:59.650 --> 00:19:01.460
What was your opinion of this target,

00:19:01.460 --> 00:19:03.010
as a former gigolo.

00:19:03.010 --> 00:19:04.690
Quite frankly, she was so easy

00:19:04.690 --> 00:19:06.450
that I was bored to death.

00:19:06.790 --> 00:19:09.900
I just used her dream of opening a bar,

00:19:09.900 --> 00:19:11.440
and she completely fell for it.

00:19:11.440 --> 00:19:13.120
Stupid woman.

00:19:13.510 --> 00:19:16.180
Why would I waste my 
time on that old lady?

00:19:16.180 --> 00:19:19.120
I could barely stand 
walking next to her.

00:19:19.370 --> 00:19:21.850
I don't know how you 
came up with the idea

00:19:21.850 --> 00:19:24.020
of pretending to go broke 
after you were a couple.

00:19:24.430 --> 00:19:27.190
Most women will do anything for money.

00:19:27.380 --> 00:19:28.880
But there are a few exceptions

00:19:29.110 --> 00:19:32.520
who have a weakness for the penniless.

00:19:33.330 --> 00:19:35.890
You're starting to look 
pretty evil yourself.

00:19:36.350 --> 00:19:37.810
At this rate, you'll pay 
off the rest in no...

00:19:39.200 --> 00:19:40.390
Wh-What's that?!

00:19:43.570 --> 00:19:44.890
B-Bro!

00:19:44.890 --> 00:19:46.050
We're under attack!

00:19:46.050 --> 00:19:47.070
Wh-What?!

00:19:47.070 --> 00:19:47.900
Which gang is it?!

00:19:48.260 --> 00:19:49.460
It's not a gang!

00:19:49.460 --> 00:19:50.400
There's only one...

00:19:54.410 --> 00:19:57.410
<b>Evil 4 Lyfe</b>

00:19:54.710 --> 00:19:57.410
You're the man who was at Otose's bar!

00:19:58.120 --> 00:19:59.380
Don't worry.

00:20:00.050 --> 00:20:02.420
You guys aren't evil.

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:05.420
You just stole money from a woman

00:20:05.420 --> 00:20:07.570
who was saving up for her dream...

00:20:08.920 --> 00:20:10.550
You fooled her into thinking you

00:20:10.550 --> 00:20:13.040
wanted to marry her so you 
could take her money...

00:20:14.440 --> 00:20:17.470
That doesn't make you evil.

00:20:18.220 --> 00:20:22.510
I'll show you what true evil looks like.

00:20:35.330 --> 00:20:37.140
Do you have a moment?

00:20:38.620 --> 00:20:40.680
I feel like having a drink.

00:20:41.190 --> 00:20:42.920
Are you open?

00:20:43.840 --> 00:20:45.420
That's a relief.

00:20:45.420 --> 00:20:47.580
I didn't think anyone

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:50.420
would be open with the snow and all.

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:53.930
Just give me one shot 
of your cheapest booze.

00:21:07.760 --> 00:21:09.900
This is a nice place.

00:21:09.900 --> 00:21:11.650
You can watch the moon, watch the snow,

00:21:11.650 --> 00:21:13.720
and have a drink.

00:21:15.880 --> 00:21:19.470
But I have one complaint.

00:21:20.970 --> 00:21:24.080
Nobody cries while pouring a drink.

00:21:26.160 --> 00:21:30.470
You have to have a smile 
on your face at all times.

00:21:32.150 --> 00:21:34.970
Even if the customer is crying.

00:21:36.750 --> 00:21:41.130
You still have much to learn, Catherine.

00:21:48.390 --> 00:21:51.480
Well, let's go have a drink.

00:21:51.810 --> 00:21:52.710
Gin-san.

00:21:52.710 --> 00:21:54.940
I brought a little present...

00:21:54.940 --> 00:21:56.030
The drinks...

00:21:57.010 --> 00:21:58.360
...are on me.

00:21:58.370 --> 00:22:02.950
<b>Catherine
Greater Edo Bank</b>

00:23:30.000 --> 00:23:39.340
<b>Next Episode</b>

00:23:34.560 --> 00:23:36.270
It's like a dream come true!

00:23:36.270 --> 00:23:37.890
I'll pretend like these 
glasses are Gin-san

00:23:37.890 --> 00:23:39.340
and never let them go!

00:23:39.340 --> 00:23:40.180
Next time:

00:23:39.340 --> 00:23:44.970
<b>Glasses Are Part of the Soul</b>

00:23:40.180 --> 00:23:42.280
Glasses are part of the soul!
